{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion","id":1416114,"title":"Vampire <> Mage Question Set [Discipline -> Spheres] Especially Chimestry/Illusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-30T09:38:21-07:00","id":1416114,"title":"Vampire <> Mage Question Set [Discipline -> Spheres] Especially Chimestry/Illusion","content":"As some of you have undoubtedly noticed, I have been asking a lof of Mage | Vampire questions. Maybe I'll write this all up after I get a little of play through done. I think I've got a lot of what I ened for a Mage living in a world of Vampires. (Like a lot of great feedback on how to imitate a Vampire as a Mage - which should be interesting to see how that works in game.)<br /> <br /> In particular, I'm curious how to imitate Disciplines with Spheres, so I put together a little map of how I think it might work. The sphere levels required would vary based on the specific disciplines.<br /> <br /> Most of them may also require some Prime. Many of the higher level disciplines will also require some Correspondence for AOE.<br /> <br /> Auspex -&gt; Prime, Mind, Spirit (Astral Projection, etc.)<br /> Celerity -&gt; Time<br /> Dementation -&gt; Mind<br /> Dominate -&gt; Mind<br /> Fortitude -&gt; Life<br /> Necromancy -&gt; Spirit<br /> Presence -&gt; Mind + Correspondence<br /> Protean -&gt; LIfe, Matter <br /> Potence -&gt; Life<br /> Obfuscate -&gt; Mind + Correspondence (as the discipline, but could also be accomplished with Forces)<br /> Quietus -&gt; Forces, Life, Prime<br /> Serpentis -&gt; This is a mishmash of stuff. but mostly Life + Prime with some Mind, Matter<br /> Thaumaturgy -&gt; Varies by Path<br /> Vicissitude -&gt; Life<br /> <br /> Big ones I have questions about<b></b>:<br /> Animalism -&gt; Mind? (Maybe Spirit for some stuff) [Can Mind control animals?]<br /> Chimestry -&gt; Forces + Mind? [I am not sure how mages create Illusions... Is it Forces 3?]<br /> <br /> I'm not sure Obtenebration fits anywhere.<br /> <br /> Any additional details or thoughts appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T09:48:45-07:00","id":1416116,"title":"","content":"You probably need some Entropy along with Spirit to \u201csimulate\u201d Necromancy. After all, that's what the necromancers in the Euthanatos Tradition Book need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T10:00:41-07:00","id":1416119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Mind control animals? </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm pretty sure it can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Chimestry -&gt; Forces + Mind? [I am not sure how mages create Illusions... Is it Forces 3?] </div> </div> </div>Something like that, yeah. You need to decide if it's going to be a psychic illusion (Mind) of a physical one (Forces - with some Prime to not have to transform the surroundings). I guess you could do both, but it's kinda redundant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obtenebration </div> </div> </div>Much of Obtenebration can be simulated trough Forces (control darkness, give it some kinetic force). But the *real deal* requires the ST to define what it's the Abyss (and the mage to know it). Spirit would be a must because it's summoning the substance (and denizens?) of another world. Corr or Prime to summon/materialize it. Entropy if it's Dark Umbra stuff. (and we know Entropy commands the spooky :P )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-30-2020, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T12:48:41-07:00","id":1416322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion#post1416114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Big ones I have questions about<b></b>:<br /> Animalism -&gt; Mind? (Maybe Spirit for some stuff) [Can Mind control animals?]<br /> Chimestry -&gt; Forces + Mind? [I am not sure how mages create Illusions... Is it Forces 3?]<br /> <br /> I'm not sure Obtenebration fits anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Chimerstry is Spirit, since, if I remember correctly, the illusions are conjured from the world of the fae.<br /> the illusions also count as real to the fae (and changelings I think)<br /> <br /> Obtenebration is also Spirit, you'd probably need forces for obtenebration 3 and Correspondence for the teleportation powers<br /> <br /> Animalism is Spirit as well, it targets the Beast and not the Mind,<br /> in VtM, animals only have instincts (beast),<br /> you may need correspondence/mind for animalism 4 and 5<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Auspex -&gt; Prime, Mind, Spirit (Astral Projection, etc.)<br /> Celerity -&gt; Time<br /> Dementation -&gt; Mind<br /> Dominate -&gt; Mind<br /> Fortitude -&gt; Life<br /> Necromancy -&gt; Spirit<br /> Presence -&gt; Mind + Correspondence<br /> Protean -&gt; LIfe, Matter<br /> Potence -&gt; Life<br /> Obfuscate -&gt; Mind + Correspondence (as the discipline, but could also be accomplished with Forces)<br /> Quietus -&gt; Forces, Life, Prime<br /> Serpentis -&gt; This is a mishmash of stuff. but mostly Life + Prime with some Mind, Matter<br /> Thaumaturgy -&gt; Varies by Path<br /> Vicissitude -&gt; Life </div> </div> </div>Vicissitude requires Life, Matter and Prime if you're using it on vampires<br /> <br /> Dominate 3 requires Time as well as Mind,<br /> in the Revised storyteller's handbook, Dominate 3 is countered by Mind+Time<br /> <br /> Potence is Forces,<br /> Potence is kinetic power, not your limbs getting stronger","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:08:37-07:00","id":1416325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion?p=1416116#post1416116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably need some Entropy along with Spirit to \u201csimulate\u201d Necromancy. After all, that's what the necromancers in the Euthanatos Tradition Book need.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be a paradigm thing though. Same way that technocrats can affect the spirit world with Matter in the convention books and dreamspeakers require spirit for all effects in &quot;How do you Do That&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T11:37:10-07:00","id":1416883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion#post1416114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chimestry -&gt; Forces + Mind? [I am not sure how mages create Illusions... Is it Forces 3?]</div> </div> </div> </div> The question you should be asking is: what <i>is </i>Chimerstry? I would argue, based on what's in various 2nd Ed. sources that were not explicitly disclaimed later, but simply not longer mentioned, that a vampire using Chimerstry is making Chimera, more or less the same as the Fae do. I'm fairly certain this is in Clabook: Ravnos (2e), and there also something about it in some 2e Changeling book--(per those sources)--chimerical weapons and object and made by a Ravnos are usable by changeling in their Fae seeming, and can do chimerical damage to changelings. Moreover, chimerical illusions dispelled from the 'real world' continue on with some kind of independent existence in the Dreaming. On the Changeling side of things, Changelings can make their arts manifest in a way that affects the real world/real things/non-glamoured or enchanted people by calling upon the &quot;Wyrd&quot; (which costs them a Willpower point), which is well beyond the capabilities of Chimerstry below 7th- or 8th-level powers (barring one Fort.3/Chim.5 combo disc. that makes inanimate objects no larger than a person). That said, the Ravnos <i>can</i> make their illusions more &quot;real&quot; by spending additional Willpower (above and beyond that necessary to even make an illusion in the first place) to enact a horrid reality and do damage. I provide these examples to show that, depending on one's proficiency with creating, manifesting, or bringing to bear &quot;chimera&quot; (i.e., the stuff dreams are literally made from), it's possible (through varying degrees of expenditures of will) to achieve a wide array of results that <i>actually</i> affect the &quot;real world.&quot; In other words, to the extent that a mage were able to just <i>generate </i>chimera (via powers that are already understood to be potent instantiations of the mage's powerful will,) it shouldn't be necessary to throw in Forces or any other such thing in order to achieve the effects that are pulled off by all manner of Chimerstry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-05T17:18:55-07:00","id":1416912,"title":"","content":"I think they said you can also use Life to Control the simplest forms of life, in the sense that it\u2019s more steering the pheromones so cause hunger or fight or flight reactions in fish and insects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T12:29:39-07:00","id":1417187,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2319_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2319\" data-vbnamecard=\"2319\">CaptOtter</a> Yeah Chimestry itself is interesting and vague in that way, like Obtenebration. I am more interested in 1. How do I generally do illusions as a Mage (which might be a whole other thread) and more relevant for this thread 2. How do I fake Chimestry if I want to pretend to be a Ravnos. This might be different if there are no Ravnos around, because any basic illusions would probably trick other vampires who haven't seen Chimestry frequently... or ever.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> Yeah based on what I read most of animalism is Mind, except the points around controlling someones beast which I guess would be Spirit?<br /> <br /> Thanks again for all the answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26423-lokitx","name":"LokiTX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T13:51:22-07:00","id":1417200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion?p=1417187#post1417187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. How do I generally do illusions as a Mage (which might be a whole other thread)</div> </div> </div> </div> Theoretically you could use Mind to make people believe they're seeing <i>whatever</i>, and it would not only appeal to all the senses, but there's probably not much poking or prodding with other sphere &quot;senses&quot; that would give up the game, if only because you could tell the affected individual's mind not only <i>what </i>to see/hear/taste/feel (i.e., sense,) but also that the illusion is <i>definitely</i> real, such that, arguably, their mind would rationalize any discrepancy in favor of maintaining that truth. However, unlike with Chimerstry (which is appears on camera because, after it all, it is a sort of <i>stuff</i>), it would exist exclusively within the mind of the individuals affected. Depending how what your ST is like, you may or may not be obligated to use Prime 2 based on the argument that you are <i>creating</i> new thoughtforms from nothing (as opposed to using Mind to <i>change</i> someone's mind or mood, or simply assert direct control over them.) The textual support for the idea that you'd need Prime 2 comes from <i>M:tA (Rev.)</i>, pg. 180, which provides under the entry for Prime 2 &quot;[t]he mage can also spin dreams, nightmares and quasi-real phantasms with Mind magic[.]&quot; This paragraph holds the creation of &quot;dreams, nightmares, and quasi-real phantasms&quot; as being <i>ejusdem generis</i> with the aspect of Prime 2 that combines with Matter and Forces to conjure those things from nothing.<br /> <br /> That said, you could also use Forces 3, Prime 2 to make auditory, visual, and tactile illusions (i.e., the holodeck). The limitation here would be gustatory (taste and smell), which you could either fill in with Mind 3 (see above, Mind really covers all the bases except photographs, video, and other recordings); or you could use Matter 3 to create the necessary aerosolized particles to create an actual taste or smell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiTX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion?p=1417187#post1417187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. How do I fake Chimestry if I want to pretend to be a Ravnos. This might be different if there are no Ravnos around, because any basic illusions would probably trick other vampires who haven't seen Chimestry frequently... or ever.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it ultimately depends on who you're trying to fool. Ravnos are as susceptible to being duped by Chimerstry as anyone, and there's nothing about the discipline that makes them any better equipped than anyone else to detect chimerical illusions. In other words, as written, Chimerstry does not appear to &quot;sing&quot; to other Chimerstry or Chimer users (though I would argue that Fae with the capacity to know how Chimera from &quot;real&quot; things would see Chimer for what it is), or, put another way, you absolutely <i>can</i> bullshit a bullshitter. That said, if you're trying to pass yourself off as a Ravnos to a real Ravnos, it probably won't matter in most cases whether you use Mind magics to simulate Chimer, or you use Forces, Matter, and Prime.<br /> <br /> Now, if you're dealing with someone with a deeper bag of tricks, who understands something about the nature of Chimerstry, chimera, the Fae, what-have-you, <i>and </i>they have the sensory modalities to conduct an actual examination of something's essence, energy, metaphysical energy, resonance, etc., well, now you may need to actually generate REAL chimerical <i>stuff</i>. This has not come up in my game, and I don't know that it's been written how a mage would go about fabricating chimera from nothing--however--I would extrapolate that Chimera is governed or affected by equal parts Mind and Spirit--not just waking nightmare phantoms or whatever (per that blurb in Mage Revised), but rather, <i>actual </i>chimera that would read like chimera to the Fae, and take on a life of its own in the dreaming, and even linger there. I'm basing this on the fact that in several places (definitely in various M20 books, and perhaps some sources in earlier editions,) it is written that healing/harming/aging/etc. Changelings requires equal parts Life and Mind (the same way that heal/harm/etc. shifters requires Life+Spirit, and vampires requires Life+Matter,) which tells me that the non-human aspect of the Changeling's nature (i.e., their Fae seeming/chimerical self) is governed by Mind. The Dreaming (though it is called a &quot;Zone&quot;) is clearly affected by the Spirit sphere, given that there are some mages who can use Spirit 3 to step sideways into the dreaming, and you probably wouldn't <i>Life</i> and Mind to affect a pure chimerical creature (because then, hat's so special about the Changeling way?) So, that's why I speculate that chimerical <i>stuff </i>is a combination of Mind + Spirit. Having said that, I wouldn't let just anyone start making chimerical objects or creatures left and right simple because they have some combination of Mind, Spirt, and Prime 2--I would, if only for intellectual honestly, require that that even be possible within their paradigm (I would argue Technocrats are out), as well as have a not insignificant amount of Fae/Changeling/Dreaming/Chimera Lore, or like Occult 4 or 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 10-07-2020, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T20:55:19-07:00","id":1417249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion?p=1416325#post1416325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That might be a paradigm thing though. Same way that technocrats can affect the spirit world with Matter in the convention books and dreamspeakers require spirit for all effects in &quot;How do you Do That&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. For example, M20 requires Spirit+Entropy to enter the Dark Umbra; is not just a paradigm thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T22:29:06-07:00","id":1417262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416114-vampire-mage-question-set-discipline-spheres-especially-chimestry-illusion?p=1417249#post1417249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, no. For example, M20 requires Spirit+Entropy to enter the Dark Umbra; is not just a paradigm thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Though if you're feeling adventurous you can also just walk there from one of the connection points in the middle umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}